{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-64874" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n2{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+22t{y}^{′}+50y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64874" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+22t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+50{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+22\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+50{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+22\\lambda +50] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+22\\lambda +50 & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}+20\\lambda +50 & =0 \\\\ 2({\\lambda }^{2}+10\\lambda +25) & =0 \\\\ 2(\\lambda +5)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-5.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64874" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50583aa4845407b20a0d1502910f2e281ea19c9e3ec0e18f6ab667bd588d3bc9"} {"question" "q-64874" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64874" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}t+{c}_{2}{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{3}+{c}_{2}{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-5}"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64874" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+13t{y}^{′}+36y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+13t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+36{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+13\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+36{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+13\\lambda +36] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+13\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+12\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +6)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-6.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-6}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50583aa4845407b20a0d1502910f2e281ea19c9e3ec0e18f6ab667bd588d3bc9"} {"question" "q-64877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-6}+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-6}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{3}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-3}"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{3}+{c}_{2}{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{6}+{c}_{2}{t}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-6}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64777" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64777" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}-x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }-\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-\\lambda +1] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-\\lambda +1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =1.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{1}+{c}_{2}{x}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64777" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50583aa4845407b20a0d1502910f2e281ea19c9e3ec0e18f6ab667bd588d3bc9"} {"question" "q-64777" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64777" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}{x}^{-1}"] ["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}{x}^{2}"] ["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-1}+{c}_{2}"] ["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64777" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(x)={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+19x{y}^{′}+81y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+19x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+81{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+19\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+81{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+19\\lambda +81] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+19\\lambda +81 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+18\\lambda +81 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +9)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-9.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-9}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c