uestion-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+10t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+8{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+10\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+8{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+10\\lambda +8] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+10\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ 2({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-2.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50583aa4845407b20a0d1502910f2e281ea19c9e3ec0e18f6ab667bd588d3bc9"} {"question" "q-64872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}t+{c}_{2}t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}t+{c}_{2}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-1}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{t}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{-2}+{c}_{2}{t}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-9x{y}^{′}+25y=0,\\,y(1)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=4,\\,x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}-9x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+25{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }-9\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+25{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-9\\lambda +25] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-9\\lambda +25 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +25 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =5.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{5}+{c}_{2}{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nSubstituting $y(1)=-2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n-2={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=4.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =5{x}^{4}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}{x}^{4}+5{c}_{2}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=4$ and ${c}_{1}=-2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =5{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 4 & =-10+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =-2{x}^{5}+14{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =2{x}^{5}(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50583aa4845407b20a0d1502910f2e281ea19c9e3ec0e18f6ab667bd588d3bc9"} {"question" "q-64883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(x)=2{x}^{5}(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)"] ["math" "y(x)=2{x}^{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)"] ["math" "y(x)=2{x}^{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2)"] ["math" "y(x)={x}^{-5}(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2)"] ["math" "y(x)={x}^{-5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-64883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(x)=2{x}^{5}(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}-17t{y}^{′}+81y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={c}_{1}{t}^{9}+{c}_{2}{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}-17t{y}^{′}+81y,\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=3,\\,t>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=0.$ Substituting $y(1)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n0={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- Then, we apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=3.$ Differentiating $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =9{c}_{1}{t}^{8}+{c}_{2}{t}^{8}+9{c}_{2}{t}^{8}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=3$ and ${c}_{1}=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =9{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 3 & =0+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =3{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50583aa4845407b20a0d1502910f2e281ea19c9e3ec0e18f6ab667bd588d3bc9"} {"question" "q-93915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(t)=-2{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)=2{t}^{9}+3{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)=3{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)=4{t}^{9}-3{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] ["math" "y(t)={t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(t)=3{t}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-102365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+15x{y}^{′}+49y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={c}_{1}{x}^{-7}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+15x{y}^{′}+49y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=1,\\,x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-102365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=1.$ Substituting $y(1)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n1={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- Then, we apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=1.$ Differentiating $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-7{c}_{1}{x}^{-8}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-8}-7{c}_{2}{x}^{-8}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ and ${c}_{1}=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-7(1)+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={x}^{-7}+8{x}^{-7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1+8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-102365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50583aa4845407b20a0d1502910f2e281ea19c9e3ec0e18f6ab667bd588d3bc9"} {"question" "q-102365" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-102365" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(x)=\\frac{1+6\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}"] ["math" "y(x)=\\frac{1+8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}"] ["math" "y(x)=\\frac{1-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}"] ["math" "y(x)=\\frac{2-12\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}"] ["math" "y(x)=\\frac{2-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-102365" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(x)=\\frac{1+8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{7}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=4,\\,x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=1.$ Substituting $y(1)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n1={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- Then, we apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=1.$ Differentiating $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ and ${c}_{1}=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =1+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x)=x+3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50583aa4845407b20a0d1502910f2e281ea19c9e3ec0e18f6ab667bd588d3bc9"} {"question" "q-93910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(x)=2x-5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "y(x)=\\frac{x}{2}-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "y(x)=x+3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "y(x)=x-4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "y(x)=x-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(x)=x+3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93912" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-7x{y}^{′}+16y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={c}_{1}{x}^{4}+{c}_{2}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-7x{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,y(1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=6,\\,x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93912" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=2.$ Substituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n2={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- Then, we apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=6.$ Differentiating $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =4{c}_{1}{x}^{3}+{c}_{2}{x}^{3}+4{c}_{2}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=6$ and ${c}_{1}=2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =4(2)+{c}_{2} \\\\ 6 & =8+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x)=2{x}^{4}-2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93912" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50583aa4845407b20a0d1502910f2e281ea19c9e3ec0e18f6ab667bd588d3bc9"} {"question" "q-93912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(x)=-2{x}^{4}+3{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "y(x)=-3{x}^{4}-4{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "y(x)=2{x}^{4}-2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "y(x)=2{x}^{4}-3{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "y(x)=2{x}^{4}-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "q-93912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(x)=2{x}^{4}-2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/state.json" "file_sha256" "39db53091a5b10d97f4772fd4106e04438bc315655263c7c3e99056c994ab7b2"} {"question" "e-6627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n2x^2 y'' + 6 xy' + 2y = 0, \\qquad x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/example-6627.json" "file_sha256" "fdf8d2d51a786e665c20e1638dcdd5526312d3d5a3054bc03ede3f3c68f6876e"} {"question" "e-6627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume the solutions take the form $y=x^\\lambda.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\ny' = \\lambda x^{\\lambda -1}, \\qquad y'' = \\lambda(\\lambda-1)x^{\\lambda-2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+6x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+2{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+6\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+2{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+6\\lambda +2] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+6\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ 2({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ 2(\\lambda +1)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation has a double root $\\lambda = -1.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={c}_{1}{x}^{-1}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{1}}{x}+\\frac{{c}_{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/example-6627.json" "file_sha256" "fdf8d2d51a786e665c20e1638dcdd5526312d3d5a3054bc03ede3f3c68f6876e"} {"question" "e-6628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\nx^2 y'' - 19 xy' + 100y = 0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny =c_1 x^{10}+ c_2x ^{10}\\ln x ,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\nx^2 y'' - 19 xy' + 100y = 0, \\quad y(1) = 0,\\quad  y'(1)=1, \\quad x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/example-6628.json" "file_sha256" "697922449ccd5385d838c85f00c8851a71b86768ab8b36151db5dbf8e1a9cdfd"} {"question" "e-6628" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $c_1$ and $c_2$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=0.$ Substituting $y(1)= 0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n0= c_1.\n$$\n\n- Then, we apply the condition $y'(1) = 1.$ Differentiating $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =10{c}_{1}{x}^{9}+{c}_{2}{x}^{9}+10{c}_{2}{x}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y'(1)=1$ and $c_1 = 0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =10{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 1 & =0+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x) = x ^{10}\\ln x .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070153/example-6628.json" "file_sha256" "697922449ccd5385d838c85f00c8851a71b86768ab8b36151db5dbf8e1a9cdfd"}] "usage" {"e-6627" [] "q-64777" [] "e-6628" []} "basis" 2447 "retractions" [[17592186152529 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$x^{2}y^{″} - xy^{′} + y = 0, x > 0$."] [17592186151890 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n$2x^2 y'' + 6 xy' + 2y = 0, \\qquad x>0$."] [17592186151890 :question/worked-solution "This is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume the solutions take the form\n\n$$\ny=x^\\lambda\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\ny' = \\lambda x^{\\lambda -1}, \\qquad y'' = \\lambda(\\lambda-1)x^{\\lambda-2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x^{2} \\cdot λ(λ - 1)x^{λ - 2} + 6x \\cdot λx^{λ - 1} + 2x^{λ} &= 0 \\\\\n2λ(λ - 1)x^{λ} + 6λx^{λ} + 2x^{λ} &= 0 \\\\\nx^{λ}[2λ(λ - 1) + 6λ + 2] &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2λ(λ - 1) + 6λ + 2 &= 0 \\\\\n2λ^{2} + 4λ + 2 &= 0 \\\\\n2(λ^{2} + 2λ + 1) &= 0 \\\\\n2(λ + 1)^{2} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation has a double root\n\n$$\n\\lambda = -1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny(x) &= c_{1}x^{-1} + c_{2}x^{-1}\\ln x \\\\\n&= \\frac{c_{1}}{x} + \\frac{c_{2}\\ln x}{x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186151891 :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$x^2 y'' - 19 xy' + 100y = 0$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$y =c_1 x^{10}+ c_2x ^{10}\\ln x$,\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$x^2 y'' - 19 xy' + 100y = 0, \\quad y(1) = 0,\\quad y'(1)=1, \\quad x>0$."] [17592186151891 :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $c_1$ and $c_2$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=0$. Substituting $y(1)= 0$ into the general solution gives\n$0= c_1$.\n- Then, we apply the condition $y'(1) = 1$. Differentiating $y$, we get\n$y^{′}|= 10c_{1}x^{9} + c_{2}x^{9} + 10c_{2}x^{9}\\ln x$.\n\nSubstituting $y'(1)=1$ and $c_1 = 0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 &= 10c_{1} + c_{2} \\\\\n1 &= 0 + c_{2} \\\\\nc_{2} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x) = x ^{10}\\ln x\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186150085 17592186150086 17592186150087 17592186150088 17592186150089] "immutable_fields" [[17592186150